Gallery, Contact\\\\n2. **Secure Portal**: Login, Dashboard, Documents, Announcements, Profile\\\\n3. **Blog System**: Posts, Categories, Archives, Admin Interface\\\\n4. **Contact Form**: Validation, Email Integration, Spam Protection\\\\n5. **Admin Panel**: User Management, Content Management, System Settings\\\\n\\\\nThis structure provides clear separation of concerns and ensures dependencies are built in the correct order. Each phase builds upon the previous one, minimizing rework and ensuring a solid foundation for subsequent features.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"DPM-001\\\"\\n}\\n###REPORT-DPM-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Director Grymm has submitted a comprehensive, high-level project plan structure, fulfilling order `DPM-001`. This framework is well-conceived and will serve as the skeleton for our final Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\n\\nHowever, I cannot proceed with the next step of the Planning phase until I receive the technology stack recommendation from Director Pryce, as per order `DTS-001`. The choice of technology is fundamental and will dictate the specific directives required for every phase of Grymm's plan.\\n\\nTherefore, I will await Director Pryce's report. As I have an outstanding order, I will not issue any new calls at this time.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###REPORT-DTS-001###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Pryce (fd085069-5bc6-4675-b42b-e195d3346633)\\nTo: d0e2efeb-6e25-4edd-83ea-6394c2f9bd6a\\nType: Reporting\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Pryce\\\\nSubject: Technology Stack Recommendation for HOA Website Project\\\\nReference Order: DTS-001\\\\n\\\\n1. Executive Summary\\\\nI recommend WordPress as the core technology for this project. It offers the most effective balance of end-user ease-of-use, required functionality, and cost-effectiveness.\\\\n\\\\n2. Analysis of Options\\\\n- WordPress: Excellent ease-of-use for a non-technical user, manageable security with proper procedures, and low cost. The ideal balance.\\\\n- Hosted Site Builders: Superior ease-of-use but carry risks of vendor lock-in, higher long-term costs, and functional limitations.\\\\n- Custom Development: Prohibitively expensive and complex. Building a simple custom CMS is a major project in itself and does not meet the cost-effectiveness requirement.\\\\n\\\\n3. Recommendation & Justification\\\\nWordPress is the optimal choice. Its CMS is industry-standard for non-technical users. The required resident portal functionality can be implemented with well-vetted membership plugins. The security risks are manageable and must be addressed with specific hardening steps in the DEP. This approach provides the best balance of user empowerment, functionality, and cost.\\\\n\\\\n4. Proposed Next Actions\\\\nUpon approval, I propose we begin detailing the WordPress-based plan. This includes selecting specific plugins for security and membership, defining the site structure, and beginning to draft the DEP with installation and configuration steps.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"DTS-001\\\"\\n}\\n###REPORT-DTS-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I have received the necessary foundational reports from both directors. Director Grymm has provided a robust project plan structure, and Director Pryce has made a sound recommendation to use WordPress as the core technology.\\n\\nThe next step in the Planning phase is to combine these elements into a detailed, step-by-step plan. To do this effectively, I require specific technical details regarding the WordPress implementation. Director Pryce is the appropriate agent to gather this information.\\n\\nTherefore, I will issue a new order to Director Pryce to research and report on the specific plugins, themes, and security protocols needed for this project. Once I receive this technical specification, I will forward it to Director Grymm to construct the final Deter